    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/TradeDetail.tsx",
      "content": "Guard these asynchronous updates against obsolete requests. If trade A's detail has loaded but its replay is delayed, navigating to trade B can finish B's reads before A's replay resolves; this continuation then replaces B with A under B's URL. The route does not key TradeDetail by tradeId. Use a request generation/cancellation guard for both the replay continuation and retry loop, and invalidate it on effect cleanup.",
      "existing_code": "        const replay = await readReplay(facade, tradeId, binding);\n        // The Workspace moved since the Detail's binding: both are read again, so the screen shows one snapshot.\n        if (replay !== 'Moved') {\n          setState({ kind: 'Ready', view, replay });",
      "start_line": 68,
      "end_line": 71,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/trade-detail/Cockpit.tsx",
      "content": "The replay-backed Journal needs to reveal the requested debt's page when handling Needs you's “Reflect now”. JournalCards only shows three cards per page, but mounts all cards with hidden on the others. OwedDebtItem consumes the context request even inside a hidden card, so a debt in an older session opens an invisible form and blocks other debt forms while the Journal remains on the current page. Pass the requested debt through to the cards and select its containing page before opening/focusing the form.",
      "existing_code": "        if (cardsReplay) return \u003cJournalCards {...shell} replay={cardsReplay} facade={facade} {...(onDirtyChange \u0026\u0026 { onDirtyChange })} /\u003e;",
      "start_line": 116,
      "end_line": 116,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
